From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:43:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: do not log a deferred PHY lookup as an error

dsi_get_phy() returns -EPROBE_DEFER while the DSI PHY driver has not
bound yet and prints "phy driver is not ready" with DRM_DEV_ERROR. With
a DisplayPort controller in the same display subsystem the probe order
of the children changes and a DSI host can come before its PHY, so every
boot shows that error although the host binds on the retry.

Use dev_err_probe() so that the deferral is recorded as the deferred
probe reason instead.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi.c | 11 +++++------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi.c
index c726fc628a08..f3ba7fac3a0c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi.c
@@ -44,14 +44,13 @@ static int dsi_get_phy(struct msm_dsi *msm_dsi)
 
 	of_node_put(phy_node);
 
-	if (!phy_pdev) {
-		DRM_DEV_ERROR(&pdev->dev, "%s: phy driver is not ready\n", __func__);
-		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
-	}
+	if (!phy_pdev)
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+				     "%s: phy driver is not ready\n", __func__);
 	if (!msm_dsi->phy) {
 		put_device(&phy_pdev->dev);
-		DRM_DEV_ERROR(&pdev->dev, "%s: phy driver is not ready\n", __func__);
-		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+				     "%s: phy driver is not ready\n", __func__);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
